WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:20.226
"Did you have fun at the apple orchard on Saturday?" Nina asked Izzie.

2
00:00:20.227 --> 00:00:23.489
They were on their way to Kids Central.

3
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:27.452
"It was so fun!" Izzie said.

4
00:00:27.453 --> 00:00:30.140
"We picked all kinds of apples.

5
00:00:30.141 --> 00:00:32.696
Green, yellow, red . . .

6
00:00:32.697 --> 00:00:38.944
And we put them in cute wooden barrels."

7
00:00:38.945 --> 00:00:44.047
The girls walked into the gym.

8
00:00:44.048 --> 00:00:50.564
"Oh! Just like those!"

9
00:00:50.565 --> 00:00:54.010
Izzie pointed to a small barrel on the table.

10
00:00:54.011 --> 00:00:56.353
It was filled with apples.

11
00:00:56.354 --> 00:00:59.705
"Welcome, girls," Miss Shelly said.

12
00:00:59.706 --> 00:01:03.017
"I went apple picking this weekend!"

13
00:01:03.018 --> 00:01:06.641
"Me too!" Izzie told their teacher.

14
00:01:06.642 --> 00:01:11.262
"The apples are for our activity today," Miss Shelly said.

15
00:01:11.263 --> 00:01:12.802
"Let me guess.

16
00:01:12.803 --> 00:01:16.610
Are we making applesauce?" Izzie asked.

17
00:01:16.611 --> 00:01:19.808
Miss Shelly grinned and shook her head.

18
00:01:19.809 --> 00:01:22.826
"Apple juice!" said Nina.

19
00:01:22.827 --> 00:01:28.598
"We're making apple stamps to decorate lunch bags," explained Miss Shelly.

20
00:01:28.599 --> 00:01:33.032
"How do you make an apple stamp?" asked Ethan.

21
00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:38.324
"You cut an apple in half and dip it in paint," Miss Shelly explained.

22
00:01:38.325 --> 00:01:41.507
"Then you can use it just like a stamp.

23
00:01:41.508 --> 00:01:44.203
First we'll stamp the lunch bags.

24
00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:48.052
Then you can glue beads and buttons on them too.

25
00:01:48.053 --> 00:01:50.790
First cut the apple in half.

26
00:01:50.791 --> 00:01:55.436
Then press the cut-side onto a paper towel to dry it off.

27
00:01:55.437 --> 00:02:03.458
Ethan, would you please pass the paper towels around?" Miss Shelly asked.

28
00:02:03.459 --> 00:02:06.685
Izzie glanced at the jars of paint.

29
00:02:06.686 --> 00:02:09.669
"What colors are we using?"

30
00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:13.312
"We have all the basic colors," Miss Shelly said.

31
00:02:13.313 --> 00:02:16.508
"If you want to make more colors, just mix them!

32
00:02:16.509 --> 00:02:18.289
Ready to start?"

33
00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:22.958
"I want to make the perfect green," Izzie thought.

34
00:02:22.959 --> 00:02:29.480
Miss Shelly passed out paper plates for the paint.

35
00:02:29.481 --> 00:02:33.332
"Press your apple into the paint.

36
00:02:33.333 --> 00:02:37.500
Then press it firmly onto the fabric," she said.

37
00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:40.356
"Hold it down for a few seconds.

38
00:02:40.357 --> 00:02:46.378
You want to make sure the whole stamp stamps!"

39
00:02:46.379 --> 00:02:49.541
Izzie poured blue paint onto her plate.

40
00:02:49.542 --> 00:02:54.002
Then she added some yellow and mixed.

41
00:02:54.003 --> 00:02:59.105
Next she added a little white.

42
00:02:59.106 --> 00:03:01.856
Finally she was ready to paint.

43
00:03:01.857 --> 00:03:05.606
She dipped her apple in the paint and stamped.

44
00:03:05.607 --> 00:03:09.300
She was pressing and pressing when her hand slipped!

45
00:03:09.301 --> 00:03:12.046
"Oh no!" she cried.

46
00:03:12.048 --> 00:03:16.350
"Ha-ha! It looks like a shooting star," Ethan said.

47
00:03:16.351 --> 00:03:19.616
"A shooting apple!" Bobby said.

48
00:03:19.617 --> 00:03:25.258
"Miss Shelly, Izzie made a cool shooting apple!" Nina said.

49
00:03:25.259 --> 00:03:29.015
"It doesn't look cool," moaned Izzie.

50
00:03:29.016 --> 00:03:31.136
"It looks dumb!"

51
00:03:31.137 --> 00:03:35.131
"Well, I think it looks cool!" said Nina.

52
00:03:35.132 --> 00:03:37.967
"I'm going to make one too!"

53
00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:44.471
"I think your apple stamp looks very artistic," said Miss Shelly.

54
00:03:44.472 --> 00:03:47.071
"Thanks," Izzie said.

55
00:03:47.072 --> 00:03:50.750
"But I'm going to make a regular stamp now."

56
00:03:50.751 --> 00:03:53.711
She stamped her bag again.

57
00:03:53.712 --> 00:03:56.308
This time it was perfect.

58
00:03:56.309 --> 00:04:03.125
"Ta-da!" Izzie held up her bag with one shooting apple and one regular apple.

59
00:04:03.126 --> 00:04:07.316
Next Izzie made a tiny stem and a leaf with beads.

60
00:04:07.317 --> 00:04:12.788
Then she wrote her name at the bottom of the bag.

61
00:04:12.789 --> 00:04:20.424
She wanted everyone to know this was her very artistic lunch bag.

62
00:04:20.425 --> 00:04:24.735
Later everyone sat on the rug munching apples.

63
00:04:24.736 --> 00:04:29.501
"Ha! This apple is a funny shape," Jason cried.

64
00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:33.229
"It's not a funny shape," Izzie said.

65
00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:36.028
She looked at Miss Shelly and smiled.

66
00:04:36.029 --> 00:04:43.881
"It's artistic."

67
00:04:43.882 --> 00:04:55.924
[caption_out@
